### IMAGE GUIDANCE

**The only image that matters is in Section 6 — the sample preview flat-lay.**

What to shoot: One complete outfit laid flat from directly above on a neutral surface (cream, white, or warm stone). Structured blazer, straight-leg trouser, a blouse, and a heel. Clean, editorial. Feels like it belongs in a Sydney lifestyle magazine.

**What not to use:** Stock photos, Indian clothing or fabrics, generic "diverse group" lifestyle shots, anything that looks like it was pulled from a template. One real, well-shot flat-lay will do more for conversion than five generic images.

Optional second image if you have it: A before/after outfit comparison on an Australian-presenting woman in a professional setting. This sits in the problem strip (Section 4) and dramatically lifts the emotional impact of that section. If you don't have this now, skip it and add it later — don't delay the launch for it.

